  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e43d696b-ee4e-42f7-83a5-8f0e709f3288-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 170px;\" /></p><p><br />In&nbsp;a strong acidic medium acid-base reaction takes place so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> group&nbsp;is converted to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>+</mo></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> group.&nbsp;Due to the formation of anilinium ion, significant meta nitroaniline&nbsp;is also formed.<br />The net reaction can be written as follows,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/49048840-55a7-49ed-a3d4-fe92f1cbf1b5-image.png\" style=\"width: 700px; height: 230px;\" /></p>",
